# [M] Implement Global Footer

## 📖 Story / Why
The footer serves as the final anchor for every page, providing essential trust signals, legal information, and quick navigation. It ensures that regardless of where a user lands, they can easily find contact details and social links, reinforcing the professional credibility required for defence and government buyers.

## 🧭 Context
- **Location:** `website/src/components/` (reusable `Footer` component).
- **Layout:** Integrated into `website/src/app/layout.tsx`.
- **Styling:** Tailwind CSS using Navy `#0e2a4d` as the primary background.
- **Content:** Data-driven approach; contact and social information should live in a configuration file (e.g., `src/lib/site-config.ts`) to avoid hardcoding.
- **Deployment:** Verified locally via `npm run dev` before static export.

## 🔑 Access & prerequisites
- **Design Assets:** The developer must request the footer design mockup/Figma link from the Manager at `/start-ticket` to ensure an exact match.
- **Logo Assets:** Use the white/light version of the logo optimized for dark backgrounds.
- **Tools:** Next.js dev environment configured.

## ✅ Scope / What to build
- [ ] **Footer Component:**
    - **Brand Section:** Logo, short company description (sourced from config).
    - **Quick Links:** Organized columns for Products, Education, Defence, About, Contact.
    - **Contact Info:** Email, Phone, and Address sourced from config.
    - **Social Links:** Icons linked to social profiles (use placeholders if URLs are not yet provided).
    - **Bottom Bar:** Copyright notice and placeholder links to Privacy Policy / Terms.
- [ ] **Responsive Layout:**
    - Stacked layout for mobile $\to$ multi-column grid for desktop.
    - Touch-friendly targets (min 44px) for all links.

## 🎯 Acceptance Criteria
- [ ] **Visual Fidelity:** Exact match to the provided design assets.
- [ ] **Contrast:** Text must pass WCAG AA contrast checks against the Navy background (reference `MASTER.md` for valid colors on navy).
- [ ] **Responsiveness:** Verified from 360px up to desktop reflow.
- [ ] **Interactions:** Consistent hover/focus states for all links.
- [ ] **Structure:** Uses semantic `<footer>` tag.

## 🖼️ UI standards
- **Design fidelity:** Reproduce the provided design exactly. Ask PM for assets at `/start-ticket`.
- **Theming:** Ensure visibility and consistency with the brand-navy theme.
- **Responsiveness:** Desktop reflow + mobile-first approach.
- **Layout:** Edge-to-edge background; content capped and centered on large screens.
- **Accessibility:** Keyboard-operable links and high color contrast.

## 🚫 Out of scope
- Creating the actual legal pages (Privacy/Terms) — only the links in the footer.

